1
00:03:37,894 --> 00:03:43,894
The Aladdin adventure continues...

2
00:07:15,789 --> 00:07:21,789
The Return of Jafar is a family, adventure,
animation film directed by Tad Stones.

3
00:10:53,684 --> 00:10:59,684
The evil Jafar escapes from the magic lamp as an all-powerful
genie, ready to plot his revenge against Aladdin.

4
00:14:31,578 --> 00:14:37,578
From battling elusive villains atop winged horses, to dodging flames inside an exploding lava pit, it's up to Aladdin -
with Princess Jasmine and the outrageously funny Genie by his side - to save the kingdom once and for all.

5
00:18:09,473 --> 00:18:15,473
Aladdin (voice), played by Scott Weinger.

6
00:21:47,368 --> 00:21:53,368
Princess Jasmine (voice), played by Linda Larkin.

7
00:25:25,263 --> 00:25:31,263
Jafar (voice), played by Jonathan Freeman.

8
00:29:03,157 --> 00:29:09,157
Iago (voice), played by Gilbert Gottfried.

9
00:32:41,052 --> 00:32:47,052
Genie (voice), played by Dan Castellaneta.

10
00:36:18,947 --> 00:36:24,947
Abu the Monkey (voice), played by Frank Welker.

11
00:39:56,842 --> 00:40:02,842
The Return of Jafar (retroactively titled Aladdin: The Return of Jafar on later releases) is a 1994 American
direct-to-video animated musical fantasy film produced by Walt Disney Pictures and Television.

12
00:43:34,736 --> 00:43:40,736
It is the first sequel to Disney's 1992 animated feature film, Aladdin, made by combining the planned
first five episodes of the Aladdin animated television series into a feature-length film.

13
00:47:12,631 --> 00:47:18,631
Released on May 20, 1994, in North America, it was the second Disney animated feature film sequel, after
The Rescuers Down Under (1990), and the first Disney direct-to-video animated feature film.

14
00:50:50,526 --> 00:50:56,526
It also marked the first American direct-to-video animated feature film.

15
00:54:28,421 --> 00:54:34,421
Gilbert Gottfried, Jonathan Freeman, Scott Weinger, Frank Welker, Brad Kane and Linda Larkin reprise their roles from
the first film, with Jason Alexander, Val Bettin, Liz Callaway, and Dan Castellaneta joining the cast.

16
00:58:06,315 --> 00:58:12,315
The film received mostly negative reviews but sold 15 million VHS tapes, grossing more than $300 million (equivalent to $636,439,156 in 2024) on
a budget of approximately $5 million (equivalent to $10,607,319 in 2024), making it one of the best-selling films on home video.

17
01:01:44,210 --> 01:01:50,210
The film explores themes of princess, middle east, magic, parrot, sultan.

18
01:05:22,105 --> 01:05:28,105
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
